WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.132
A writing agent that remembers your work.

00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:06.777
Memoket Note brings the notes you already have into an agent-native writing workspace.

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.139
Start with three fictional Maple project notes.

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:14.708
Import creates local notes and uses a real model to extract fourteen facts.

00:00:14.788 --> 00:00:17.789
Notion and Apple Notes are also available connections.

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:20.650
The knowledge survives a backend restart.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.049
Search for shelf labels, open a remembered fact, and inspect the dated original words.

00:00:26.129 --> 00:00:29.493
This memory stays in the library across notes and sessions.

00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:33.336
Set a goal, audience, and completion criteria.

00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:35.988
Related memory appears beside the new draft.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:40.150
Add relevant facts to Materials so the agent can prioritize them.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:44.570
Smart Continue retrieves context and writes from the saved sources.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.818
The writing agent harness runs checks and keeps the changes available for review.

00:00:48.898 --> 00:00:51.135
This draft cites ten stored facts.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.056
Review still matters.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:58.252
In this run, the reviewer removes a repeated title and corrects an unsupported timing claim.

00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:02.042
A source link opens the original evidence and the backlink to the draft.

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:05.696
Download the reviewed draft as Markdown without an account.

00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:08.021
Or write it into a separate Obsidian vault.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:11.888
Both exports preserve the draft and its ten source identifiers.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.421
Bring your notes.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.635
Keep your workflow.

00:01:14.715 --> 00:01:19.432
Memoket Note is a personal open-source project built on the Memoket KITE memory engine.
